00:39:28.200 --> 00:39:30.630
This is a fundamental limitation of the human brain.

1045
00:39:30.630 --> 00:39:32.491
The human brain has not significantly changed

1046
00:39:32.491 --> 00:39:34.080
in the last 40,000 years.

1047
00:39:34.080 --> 00:39:36.400
It ain't gonna change on any time scale we gonna see.

1048
00:39:36.400 --> 00:39:38.718
You can only think about one or two things at a time.

1049
00:39:38.718 --> 00:39:42.210
But what's happened is we've fallen as a culture

1050
00:39:42.210 --> 00:39:43.560
for a mass delusion.

1051
00:39:43.560 --> 00:39:45.450
The average teenager now believes they can follow

1052
00:39:45.450 --> 00:39:48.050
six or seven forms of media at the same time.

1053
00:39:48.050 --> 00:39:48.883
So what happens is...

1054
00:39:48.883 --> 00:39:50.430
And this has been studied a huge amount.

1055
00:39:50.430 --> 00:39:52.540
Scientists get people into labs and they get them to think

1056
00:39:52.540 --> 00:39:54.220
they're doing more than one thing at a time.

1057
00:39:54.220 --> 00:39:57.520
And what they discover every time is the same thing.

1058
00:39:57.520 --> 00:39:59.010
You're not doing more than one thing at a time,

1059
00:39:59.010 --> 00:40:03.160
you're very rapidly juggling between the tasks.

1060
00:40:03.160 --> 00:40:05.540
And your consciousness kind of papers over it

1061
00:40:05.540 --> 00:40:06.373
so you don't...

1062
00:40:06.373 --> 00:40:07.720
You feel like you're doing the things

1063
00:40:07.720 --> 00:40:09.480
at the same time but you're not.

1064
00:40:09.480 --> 00:40:11.550
And what they find is when you try and do

1065
00:40:11.550 --> 00:40:13.840
more than one thing at a time,

1066
00:40:13.840 --> 00:40:16.850
something called the switch cost effect kicks in.

1067
00:40:16.850 --> 00:40:18.550
Everyone should know this term, the switch cost effect

1068
00:40:18.550 --> 00:40:20.730
'cause it's harming your life.

1069
00:40:20.730 --> 00:40:22.290
The switch cost effect shows,

1070
00:40:22.290 --> 00:40:24.450
when you try and do more than one thing at a time

1071
00:40:24.450 --> 00:40:26.360
you will do all the things

1072
00:40:26.360 --> 00:40:28.810
you're trying to do much less competently.

1073
00:40:28.810 --> 00:40:30.330
You'll make more mistakes,

1074
00:40:30.330 --> 00:40:32.270
you'll remember less of what you do,

1075
00:40:32.270 --> 00:40:33.950
you'll be less creative.

1076
00:40:33.950 --> 00:40:36.300
And this feels like a small effect when you hear about it.

1077
00:40:36.300 --> 00:40:38.580
You (indistinct), "Yeah, okay, I get it."

1078
00:40:38.580 --> 00:40:40.350
But how big can that be?

1079
00:40:40.350 --> 00:40:41.183
The effect...

1080
00:40:41.183 --> 00:40:42.016
It shocked me when I learned about it.

1081
00:40:42.016 --> 00:40:43.990
The effect is enormous.

1082
00:40:43.990 --> 00:40:46.480
I'll give you two examples of just small studies

1083
00:40:46.480 --> 00:40:49.860
backed by much wider body of evidence that have found this.

1084
00:40:49.860 --> 00:40:52.700
Hewlett-Packard, the printer company got a scientist

1085
00:40:52.700 --> 00:40:54.680
into study their workforce

1086
00:40:54.680 --> 00:40:56.117
and they split their workers into two groups.

1087
00:40:56.117 --> 00:40:58.890
And the first group was told, "Just get on with your task,

1088
00:40:58.890 --> 00:41:01.740
whatever it is and you're not gonna be interrupted."

1089
00:41:01.740 --> 00:41:04.420
And the second group was told, "Get on with your task,

1090
00:41:04.420 --> 00:41:05.400
but you're gonna have to answer

1091
00:41:05.400 --> 00:41:08.820
a fairly heavy amount of email and phone calls."

1092
00:41:08.820 --> 00:41:11.780
So pretty much how most of us live our lives.

1093
00:41:11.780 --> 00:41:15.020
And then at the end of it they tested the IQ of both groups.

1094
00:41:15.020 --> 00:41:18.890
The group that had not been interrupted scored on average

1095
00:41:18.890 --> 00:41:21.374
10 IQ points higher than the group

1096
00:41:21.374 --> 00:41:22.207
that have been interrupted.

1097
00:41:22.207 --> 00:41:24.420
To give you a sense of how big an effect that is now.

1098
00:41:24.420 --> 00:41:27.480
If you get stoned your IQ goes down in the short term

1099
00:41:27.480 --> 00:41:28.830
by five points.

1100
00:41:28.830 --> 00:41:33.400
So being chronically distracted is twice as bad for your IQ,

1101
00:41:33.400 --> 00:41:35.540
your intelligence in the short term

1102
00:41:35.540 --> 00:41:36.450
as getting stoned, right?

1103
00:41:36.450 --> 00:41:37.350
That's a big effect.

1104
00:41:37.350 --> 00:41:38.670
Or look at another example,

1105
00:41:38.670 --> 00:41:40.680
Professor Larry Rosen discovered if you receive

1106
00:41:40.680 --> 00:41:43.170
eight text messages an hour which doesn't sound like

1107
00:41:43.170 --> 00:41:44.670
very much to me.

1108
00:41:44.670 --> 00:41:46.780
That lowers your brain power for the main thing

1109
00:41:46.780 --> 00:41:49.580
you're trying to focus on by 30%.

1110
00:41:49.580 --> 00:41:51.020
These are huge effects.

1111
00:41:51.020 --> 00:41:54.700
I would argue with most of us are losing about 30%.

1112
00:41:54.700 --> 00:41:55.533
Yeah.

1113
00:41:55.533 --> 00:41:56.510
Most of the time.

1114
00:41:56.510 --> 00:41:57.527
This is why professor Miller said to me,

1115
00:41:57.527 --> 00:41:59.330
"We are living in a perfect storm

1116
00:41:59.330 --> 00:42:01.240
of cognitive degradation at the moment

1117
00:42:01.240 --> 00:42:04.110
as a result of constant distraction."

1118
00:42:04.110 --> 00:42:05.570
And there's kind of two levels of which

1119
00:42:05.570 --> 00:42:06.403
we can respond to this.

1120
