while the scrolling of course, and all of that.

1189
00:44:24.820 --> 00:44:28.020
So I've witnessed firsthand this dynamic

1190
00:44:28.020 --> 00:44:32.040
and it's hugely problematic because it is on some level

1191
00:44:32.040 --> 00:44:34.620
implicitly informing them that they can do

1192
00:44:34.620 --> 00:44:38.470
all of these things well or fine at the same time

1193
00:44:38.470 --> 00:44:39.600
which is an illusion.

1194
00:44:39.600 --> 00:44:43.780
And anybody who's tried to sit down and execute

1195
00:44:43.780 --> 00:44:46.290
on a project particularly creative people.

1196
00:44:46.290 --> 00:44:49.120
I mean, the easiest example is writing a book.

1197
00:44:49.120 --> 00:44:51.580
If you're in that state and you're focused

1198
00:44:51.580 --> 00:44:55.510
and you are experiencing a certain level of flow.

1199
00:44:55.510 --> 00:44:58.390
In that process you're doing a painting or a sculpture,

1200
00:44:58.390 --> 00:45:00.705
or writing a song or whatever it is.

1201
00:45:00.705 --> 00:45:05.705
And you get interrupted that switch cost effect

1202
00:45:07.250 --> 00:45:08.110
is very real.

1203
00:45:08.110 --> 00:45:10.020
Like you've experienced that because it's not like,

1204
00:45:10.020 --> 00:45:10.970
oh, I got interrupted.

1205
00:45:10.970 --> 00:45:12.400
Even if it's someone knocks on your door

1206
00:45:12.400 --> 00:45:14.370
and says, hey, can you...

1207
00:45:14.370 --> 00:45:17.000
Don't forget to go to the grocery store or whatever.

1208
00:45:17.000 --> 00:45:19.500
The amount of time it takes to get back

1209
00:45:19.500 --> 00:45:20.710
into that flow state,

1210
00:45:20.710 --> 00:45:22.320
you can't just switch it on and off.

1211
00:45:22.320 --> 00:45:23.270
Like you...

1212
