I can't really find it."

3098
01:55:47.700 --> 01:55:50.850
It's very difficult to guide that person.

3099
01:55:50.850 --> 01:55:54.400
And I think it's somewhat...

3100
01:55:56.000 --> 01:55:57.100
what's the right word?

3101
01:55:58.595 --> 01:56:01.453
Not irresponsible, but just sort of insufficient

3102
01:56:03.660 --> 01:56:05.470
to just say, well, try a bunch of things,

3103
01:56:05.470 --> 01:56:07.870
or I trust you that you'll find it.

3104
01:56:07.870 --> 01:56:11.200
And I think what happens over time with COVID

3105
01:56:11.200 --> 01:56:14.470
really truncating people's ability to kind of explore

3106
01:56:14.470 --> 01:56:16.430
other avenues for their life is that there

3107
01:56:16.430 --> 01:56:19.140
is a sense of desperation that ensues

3108
01:56:19.140 --> 01:56:21.230
that makes it even more difficult

3109
01:56:21.230 --> 01:56:24.330
to lift yourself out of that fog or put the phone down,

3110
01:56:24.330 --> 01:56:27.330
or stop playing the game or get off the porn.

3111
01:56:27.330 --> 01:56:31.280
And it becomes this prison that becomes very difficult

3112
01:56:31.280 --> 01:56:32.630
for people to break out of.

3113
01:56:33.670 --> 01:56:34.503
I think that's true.

3114
01:56:34.503 --> 01:56:36.494
And I think we have to look at

3115
01:56:36.494 --> 01:56:40.770
the deeper reasons for that.

3116
01:56:40.770 --> 01:56:42.201
So if we think about...

3117
01:56:42.201 --> 01:56:44.030
We just talked about really important one, Rich,

3118
01:56:44.030 --> 01:56:46.980
which is about our ability to create meaning,

3119
01:56:46.980 --> 01:56:48.160
and find meaning.

3120
01:56:48.160 --> 01:56:51.170
And I think there's a kind of structural thing

3121
01:56:51.170 --> 01:56:52.990
that's happening to us

3122
01:56:52.990 --> 01:56:57.990
which is the destruction of our ability to....

3123
01:56:58.480 --> 01:57:01.270
Or the profound corrosion of our ability

3124
01:57:01.270 --> 01:57:02.387
to construct meaning.

3125
01:57:02.387 --> 01:57:04.680
And I wrote about this in Lost Connections

3126
01:57:04.680 --> 01:57:07.340
and we touched on it a little bit last time we spoke

3127
01:57:07.340 --> 01:57:10.027
but everyone knows that junk food has taken over our diets

3128
01:57:10.027 --> 01:57:11.730
and made us physically sick, right?

3129
01:57:11.730 --> 01:57:14.600
As you can see from my chins I'm not immune to that myself.

3130
01:57:14.600 --> 01:57:17.980
But a kind of junk values have taken over our societies

3131
01:57:17.980 --> 01:57:20.120
and our minds have made us mentally sick.

3132
01:57:20.120 --> 01:57:21.620
There's a guy called Professor Tim Kasser,

3133
01:57:21.620 --> 01:57:24.680
who's at Knox collagen in Illinois, retired now.

3134
01:57:24.680 --> 01:57:26.480
Who did lots of research on this.

3135
01:57:26.480 --> 01:57:28.560
So for 1000s of amazing research on it.

3136
01:57:28.560 --> 01:57:31.350
For 1000s of years philosophers said,

3137
01:57:31.350 --> 01:57:34.210
If you think life is about money and status

3138
01:57:34.210 --> 01:57:36.820
and showing off you're gonna feel like, right?

3139
01:57:36.820 --> 01:57:38.240
It's not an exact quote from Confucius,

3140
01:57:38.240 --> 01:57:39.890
but that's basically what he said.

3141
01:57:39.890 --> 01:57:42.360
But weirdly nobody had scientifically investigated

3142
01:57:42.360 --> 01:57:44.010
this until Professor Kasser

3143
01:57:44.010 --> 01:57:46.160
did a huge amount of research into it.

3144
01:57:46.160 --> 01:57:48.290
And he discovered that the philosophers were right.

3145
01:57:48.290 --> 01:57:50.160
That the more you think life is about money

3146
01:57:50.160 --> 01:57:52.350
and status and showing off,

3147
01:57:52.350 --> 01:57:55.280
the more likely you are to become depressed and anxious

3148
01:57:55.280 --> 01:57:56.883
by a really significant amount.

3149
01:57:57.770 --> 01:57:59.520
But what's happened is as a society,

3150
01:57:59.520 --> 01:58:02.430
we have become much more driven by those beliefs

3151
01:58:02.430 --> 01:58:04.480
in the last 40 years, right?

3152
01:58:04.480 --> 01:58:07.507
I mean, they dominate things like Instagram.

3153
01:58:07.507 --> 01:58:09.210
Think about the values of Instagram,

3154
01:58:09.210 --> 01:58:10.043
what they are?

3155
01:58:10.043 --> 01:58:11.680
The implicit values of Instagram.

3156
01:58:11.680 --> 01:58:14.390
But they dominate the whole society.

3157
01:58:14.390 --> 01:58:15.327
You talk to kids what's your goal?

3158
01:58:15.327 --> 01:58:16.567
"I wanna be a billionaire."

3159
01:58:16.567 --> 01:58:17.497
"Would you you wanna be millionaire?

3160
01:58:17.497 --> 01:58:19.100
"Just wanna be a billionaire, right?"

3161
01:58:19.100 --> 01:58:22.340
We've been taught...

3162
01:58:22.340 --> 01:58:26.050
it's almost like we've been fed a kind of KFC for the soul.

3163
01:58:26.050 --> 01:58:27.680
We've been trained to look for happiness

3164
01:58:27.680 --> 01:58:30.170
in all the wrong places through

3165
01:58:30.170 --> 01:58:32.290
working hard at jobs we don't like,

3166
01:58:32.290 --> 01:58:33.830
to buy shit we don't need,

3167
01:58:33.830 --> 01:58:36.690
to display it on social media to make people jealous.

3168
01:58:36.690 --> 01:58:38.210
And so people have been given a script

3169
01:58:38.210 --> 01:58:40.050
for how to be happy, right?

3170
01:58:40.050 --> 01:58:42.210
That's what we're told makes you feel good.

3171
01:58:42.210 --> 01:58:45.010
They do it, it doesn't make them feel good.

3172
01:58:45.010 --> 01:58:45.843
And they're like,

3173
01:58:45.843 --> 01:58:46.770
"Well, there must be something wrong with me

3174
01:58:46.770 --> 01:58:49.350
'cause I'm doing the stuff you're meant to do to be happy."

3175
01:58:49.350 --> 01:58:51.470
And at some level we know this isn't true, right?

3176
01:58:51.470 --> 01:58:54.080
No one watching thinks they're gonna lie on their death bed

3177
01:58:54.080 --> 01:58:56.370
and think about all the likes they got on Instagram

3178
01:58:56.370 --> 01:58:58.010
and all the shoes they bought, right?

3179
01:58:58.010 --> 01:58:58.843
That's not gonna be.

3180
01:58:58.843 --> 01:58:59.860
You're gonna think about moments of love

3181
01:58:59.860 --> 01:59:01.510
and meaning and connect.

3182
01:59:01.510 --> 01:59:05.360
And something that really helped me during COVID,

3183
01:59:05.360 --> 01:59:08.280
was learning from an experiment that Professor Kasser did

3184
01:59:08.280 --> 01:59:11.786
with a colleague of his Nathan Dungan.

3185
01:59:11.786 --> 01:59:14.330
And it's something I really recommend everyone do

3186
01:59:14.330 --> 01:59:16.596
if they were interested in that rediscovery in meaning

3187
01:59:16.596 --> 01:59:18.650
that you're talking about that's so important.

3188
01:59:18.650 --> 01:59:19.647
There's lots of things we can do about this

3189
01:59:19.647 --> 01:59:21.705
but this is one example.

3190
01:59:21.705 --> 01:59:22.947
So Nathan was a...

3191
01:59:22.947 --> 01:59:25.733
And he is a financial advisor in Minneapolis,

3192
01:59:27.070 --> 01:59:27.903
and he was...

3193
01:59:27.903 --> 01:59:30.620
So he advises people on like household budgets.

3194
01:59:30.620 --> 01:59:33.440
And he was contacted one day by a school,

3195
01:59:33.440 --> 01:59:34.273
a kind of middle class,

3196
01:59:34.273 --> 01:59:36.970
high school in Minneapolis.

3197
01:59:36.970 --> 01:59:38.940
And they said, "Look, we've got a real problem.

3198
01:59:38.940 --> 01:59:40.210
We need some help."

3199
01:59:40.210 --> 01:59:42.860
The kids at that school were becoming obsessed

3200
01:59:42.860 --> 01:59:46.770
with getting the latest Nike sneakers, the latest iPhone.

3201
01:59:46.770 --> 01:59:48.120
And often their parents couldn't afford it

3202
01:59:48.120 --> 01:59:49.450
and the kids were just losing their shit

3203
01:59:49.450 --> 01:59:50.910
if they couldn't get it, right?

3204
01:59:50.910 --> 01:59:51.810
And they said, "Will you come in

3205
01:59:51.810 --> 01:59:54.370
and explain budgeting to these kids?"

3206
01:59:54.370 --> 01:59:56.580
So he came in and quickly realized these kids

3207
01:59:56.580 --> 01:59:57.794
didn't give a shit about budgeting, right?

3208
01:59:57.794 --> 01:59:58.627
(chuckles)

3209
01:59:58.627 --> 01:59:59.460
He would explain budgeting and they'd be like,

3210
01:59:59.460 --> 02:00:01.910
"Yeah, whatever I need the iPhone."

3211
02:00:01.910 --> 02:00:03.946
And so what he did was a different experiment.

3212
02:00:03.946 --> 02:00:06.100
He learned about Professor Kasser's work

3213
02:00:06.100 --> 02:00:07.020
and teamed up with him.

3214
02:00:07.020 --> 02:00:09.990
And they did this really interesting experiment.

3215
02:00:09.990 --> 02:00:13.050
They got the kids and their parents to come to meetings.

3216
02:00:13.050 --> 02:00:15.210
I think if I remember rightly it was once

3217
02:00:15.210 --> 02:00:17.060
every couple of weeks for six months.

3218
02:00:18.850 --> 02:00:21.557
And the first time they met, they literally said to them,

3219
02:00:21.557 --> 02:00:24.077
"Just write a list of everything you've got to have."

3220
02:00:24.077 --> 02:00:25.560
And they didn't define what that meant.

3221
02:00:25.560 --> 02:00:26.543
People said, "What does it mean?"

3222
02:00:26.543 --> 02:00:28.060
They say, "Do whatever you think that means."

3223
02:00:28.060 --> 02:00:29.750
And of course, everyone says, first you need food.

3224
02:00:29.750 --> 02:00:32.240
You need house, whatever home.

3225
02:00:32.240 --> 02:00:33.880
But quite quickly people started to name things

3226
02:00:33.880 --> 02:00:36.100
you haven't gotta have like the latest iPhone,

3227
02:00:36.100 --> 02:00:37.400
the parents would often name things

3228
02:00:37.400 --> 02:00:40.310
that no reasonable person has to have, right?

3229
02:00:40.310 --> 02:00:43.130
Then they said to them, "Describe how you would...

3230
02:00:43.130 --> 02:00:45.900
Your life would be different if you got this thing."

3231
02:00:45.900 --> 02:00:47.950
So let's say the kids who talked about Nike sneakers,

3232
02:00:47.950 --> 02:00:49.850
how much they wanted the Nike sneakers.

3233
02:00:49.850 --> 02:00:52.350
What's interesting is none of the kids

3234
02:00:52.350 --> 02:00:54.090
gave the apparent reason for Nike sneakers.

3235
02:00:54.090 --> 02:00:56.860
None of them said, oh, I'm a basketball player

3236
02:00:56.860 --> 02:00:57.790
and I wanna be able to jump high.

3237
02:00:57.790 --> 02:00:58.870
No one said that.

3238
02:00:58.870 --> 02:01:00.860
They said things like, "Well, if I got the sneakers,

3239
02:01:00.860 --> 02:01:02.527
people would envy me."

3240
02:01:02.527 --> 02:01:05.080
people want me to be in, in their group, right?

3241
02:01:05.080 --> 02:01:06.980
Doesn't take long to get people to say this out loud

3242
02:01:06.980 --> 02:01:08.430
before they realize, oh,

3243
02:01:08.430 --> 02:01:09.490
who put that idea in your head

3244
02:01:09.490 --> 02:01:12.670
that having a little blue tick on your shoe

3245
02:01:12.670 --> 02:01:16.290
means you deserve to have friends, right?

3246
02:01:16.290 --> 02:01:18.140
But what's the most interesting bit was what happened next,

3247
02:01:18.140 --> 02:01:21.090
where they said to them, "Okay, write about...

3248
02:01:21.090 --> 02:01:22.830
Just discuss among yourselves and write about

3249
02:01:22.830 --> 02:01:24.440
a moment in your life

3250
02:01:24.440 --> 02:01:27.590
when you've had a sense of meaning and purpose."

3251
02:01:27.590 --> 02:01:29.140
Different people name different things, right?

3252
02:01:29.140 --> 02:01:29.973
We can...

3253
02:01:29.973 --> 02:01:32.546
I'll just say anyone watching just picture something now.

3254
02:01:32.546 --> 02:01:33.850
And they talked about it.

3255
02:01:33.850 --> 02:01:36.350
Whether it was taking their kids to the beach, writing,

3256
02:01:36.350 --> 02:01:38.670
playing music, whatever it might be.

3257
02:01:38.670 --> 02:01:41.530
And then he said, "Well, how can you build more of your life

3258
02:01:41.530 --> 02:01:43.700
around these moments of meaning and purpose

3259
02:01:43.700 --> 02:01:46.620
and less around the junk values,

3260
02:01:46.620 --> 02:01:48.430
which I think are a bit like junk food.

3261
02:01:48.430 --> 02:01:51.460
That we are kind of inculcated

3262
02:01:51.460 --> 02:01:52.910
in this culture all the time?"

3263
02:01:52.910 --> 02:01:53.760
And what was fascinating was,

3264
02:01:53.760 --> 02:01:55.760
so they just met every couple of weeks

3265
02:01:55.760 --> 02:01:57.750
and talked about their progress in moving away

3266
02:01:57.750 --> 02:01:58.590
from the junk values

3267
02:01:58.590 --> 02:02:00.567
and towards meaningful values.

3268
02:02:00.567 --> 02:02:02.313
And what they found was just having these conversations.

3269
02:02:02.313 --> 02:02:05.920
We don't have these conversations very often in our culture,

3270
02:02:05.920 --> 02:02:09.200
just having these conversations led to a marked move

3271
02:02:09.200 --> 02:02:10.260
in people's values, right?

3272
02:02:10.260 --> 02:02:11.590
It really worked.

3273
02:02:11.590 --> 02:02:12.954
And the reason I mentioned that in relation

3274
02:02:12.954 --> 02:02:16.112
to what you're saying, Rich is throughout COVID,

3275
02:02:16.112 --> 02:02:18.600
in fact, before COVID but during COVID as well.

3276
02:02:18.600 --> 02:02:21.200
So once month I have two of my friends

3277
02:02:21.200 --> 02:02:23.020
and first day of the month

3278
02:02:23.020 --> 02:02:24.180
we just have these conversations.

3279
02:02:24.180 --> 02:02:26.420
We talk about what happened in the last month

3280
02:02:26.420 --> 02:02:29.140
that was meaningful and what were times

3281
02:02:29.140 --> 02:02:31.380
when you were diverted onto junk values

3282
02:02:31.380 --> 02:02:32.970
and what in the next month do you wanna look for?

3283
02:02:32.970 --> 02:02:34.960
And obviously, we've been doing it on Zoom

3284
02:02:34.960 --> 02:02:35.939
'cause of the plague.

3285
02:02:35.939 --> 02:02:37.900
And even now I really feel it, right?

3286
02:02:37.900 --> 02:02:39.727
I've got this book that just came out, right?

3287
02:02:39.727 --> 02:02:41.990
And I can totally feel there's two sets of values

3288
02:02:41.990 --> 02:02:43.220
I can get into.

3289
02:02:43.220 --> 02:02:46.420
I can get into, oh, I think the things I learned

3290
02:02:46.420 --> 02:02:49.740
for Stolen Focus will help people, right?

3291
02:02:49.740 --> 02:02:51.690
And I think if other people learn about this

3292
02:02:51.690 --> 02:02:53.780
we can change things and make the world better.

3293
02:02:53.780 --> 02:02:55.370
When I think about that I feel really good.

3294
02:02:55.370 --> 02:02:56.770
I go, "Oh, yeah, I met these amazing people.

3295
02:02:56.770 --> 02:02:58.422
I just told Rich about Lenore.

3296
02:02:58.422 --> 02:03:00.160
Lenore is an amazing person.

3297
02:03:00.160 --> 02:03:01.290
I feel really glad.

3298
02:03:01.290 --> 02:03:02.770
Hope people go and look up Lenore

3299
02:03:02.770 --> 02:03:03.920
and join her group, right?

3300
02:03:03.920 --> 02:03:05.290
That makes me feel good.

3301
02:03:05.290 --> 02:03:08.260
Or I can get into who's buying the fucking book?

3302
02:03:08.260 --> 02:03:09.703
What do the reviews say, right?

3303
02:03:09.703 --> 02:03:12.326
Who are the famous people who tweeted about it, right?

3304
02:03:12.326 --> 02:03:15.240
And when I get into that zone I feel like shit

3305
02:03:15.240 --> 02:03:17.070
even when the news is good, right?

3306
02:03:17.070 --> 02:03:18.367
Even when it's I or a book selling really well

3307
02:03:18.367 --> 02:03:20.130
and this famous person just tweeted (indistinct)

3308
02:03:20.130 --> 02:03:21.270
even then feel like shit

3309
02:03:21.270 --> 02:03:23.450
because that's a junk value, right?

3310
02:03:23.450 --> 02:03:24.360
It's not...

3311
02:03:25.389 --> 02:03:26.770
It doesn't mean anything, right?

3312
02:03:26.770 --> 02:03:28.100
Whereas the meaningful stuff is,

3313
02:03:28.100 --> 02:03:31.350
oh, this person might be helped by this thing.

3314
02:03:31.350 --> 02:03:32.462
that's meaningful.

3315
02:03:32.462 --> 02:03:34.487
The ego stuff is not gonna help me, right?

3316
02:03:34.487 --> 02:03:36.193
But the problem is the ego stuff

3317
02:03:36.193 --> 02:03:40.530
and the junk value stuff is so intoxicating.

3318
02:03:40.530 --> 02:03:41.560
It's the difference.

3319
02:03:41.560 --> 02:03:44.420
It's the way that it has the pull and the allure

3320
02:03:44.420 --> 02:03:46.640
of the junk food where the fruits

3321
02:03:46.640 --> 02:03:48.491
and the vegetables don't give you...

3322
02:03:48.491 --> 02:03:49.590
(Johann laughs)

3323
02:03:49.590 --> 02:03:53.870
There isn't like that magnetic pull to them

3324
02:03:53.870 --> 02:03:55.570
and that's the war that you have to wage

3325
02:03:55.570 --> 02:03:56.580
and that's the battle.

3326
02:03:56.580 --> 02:03:57.930
I think there's two thing...

3327
02:03:57.930 --> 02:03:59.540
There's two layers to that isn't there.

3328
02:03:59.540 --> 02:04:00.373
You're totally right.

3329
02:04:00.373 --> 02:04:02.030
There's a degree to which this is just a perennial

3330
02:04:02.030 --> 02:04:03.560
human problem that will always exist, right?

3331
02:04:03.560 --> 02:04:05.530
There's always the temptation of ego

3332
02:04:05.530 --> 02:04:08.860
and the temptation of meaning, right?

3333
02:04:08.860 --> 02:04:10.880
More meaningful things.

3334
02:04:10.880 --> 02:04:13.350
But I also think that the way Professor Kasser

3335
02:04:13.350 --> 02:04:14.317
put it to me is,

3336
02:04:14.317 --> 02:04:16.900
"We live in a machine that is designed

3337
02:04:16.900 --> 02:04:19.100
to get us to neglect what is important about life."

3338
02:04:19.100 --> 02:04:21.150
So there's all this evidence, exposure to advertising

3339
02:04:21.150 --> 02:04:22.860
makes you more egotistical, right?

3340
02:04:22.860 --> 02:04:25.653
We are bombarded with advertising.

3341
02:04:26.630 --> 02:04:29.450
More 18 month old children know what the McDonald's M means,

3342
02:04:29.450 --> 02:04:32.120
they know their own last name in this country, right?

3343
02:04:32.120 --> 02:04:34.390
So you think about from when we're very young,

3344
02:04:34.390 --> 02:04:35.840
we've fed this script.

3345
02:04:35.840 --> 02:04:37.510
Says a degree to which is a perennial human problem

3346
02:04:37.510 --> 02:04:39.860
it will always be a problem and always a struggle.

3347
02:04:39.860 --> 02:04:42.320
But then in the environment in which we currently live,

3348
02:04:42.320 --> 02:04:45.061
we are loaded towards the bad choice, right?

3349
02:04:45.061 --> 02:04:48.860
Whether it's junk food, the constant distraction,

3350
02:04:48.860 --> 02:04:50.100
or the junk values,

3351
02:04:50.100 --> 02:04:51.690
we're we are living in an environment

3352
02:04:51.690 --> 02:04:55.030
that is pushing us in so many ways towards the things

3353
02:04:55.030 --> 02:04:58.300
that at some level we know are not good for our attention,

3354
02:04:58.300 --> 02:05:00.790
our depression, our addiction.

